. Most of the features are handled in this way. If it is a relatively large feature which have impacts on multiple top-level sections, e.g., NR-U, RedCap, NTN, etc., it is captured in separated sub-sections under corresponding requirements. We think this approach can also be used in 6G. It is worthy of noting that if suffix is used for the new sub-sections, same suffix should be used on all the sub-sections for the feature. Proposal 6: New features introduced in later releases are captured either by incorporating in existing section(s) or by creating new sub-sections. Same suffix should be used for the same feature in different sub-sections. One another aspect that would be considered for RRM specification improvement is to split RRM spec into two parts, one for core part and another for performance part. By further considering good drafting rules, new tools for tabulated requirements etc., the spec size and quality can be improved. It would provide good experience for the reader. Proposal 7: RAN4 to consider split RRM spec into two files for core part and performance part, respectively.

