 7.1C.2.1-1) gives a worst-case Te_floor + 200 ms drift of 0.34 µs, exceeding CP/2. Inequality (II) cannot be held at 120 kHz SCS in the worst case by Tq_NTN / Tp_NTN choice alone. Proposal #6: RAN4 to study the impact of Solution 2E on the TS 38.133 Section 7.1C.2.1 Tq_NTN / Tp_NTN parameters, with UE velocity class as candidate scope key. Specific values and any required UE-side velocity-classification mechanism under GNSS loss are FFS. Proposal #7: RAN4 to study the impact of Solution 2D on the TS 38.133 Section 7.1C.2.1 Tq_NTN / Tp_NTN parameters, with orbit class and |Δp| as candidate scope keys. GEO at the studied |Δp| range does not require parameter changes. Specific values are FFS. Proposal #8: RAN4 to study the FR2 120 kHz SCS structural limit on inequality (II), with Te_floor reduction as the required lever. Impacted TS: TS 38.133 Section 7.1C.2.1 (revised Tq_NTN / Tp_NTN requirement, conditional on finer TAC quantisation being available). TAC step definition in TS 38.213 Section 4.2 is RAN1 scope. Specific values are FFS. - TA Trigger Criterion (TS 38.213) Observation #12: Under GNSS loss, the current TA trigger |T_UL(t+Δt) − T_UL(t)| ≥ Tp_NTN loses its link to the residual UL timing error at the gNB because the UE-specific component N_TA,adj^UE freezes at the last GNSS fix. The UE can satisfy the condition while error grows, or fail to trigger when adjustment is needed.

